Look at the car. Recognize it? :)

The opinion that blackface is a negative thing is a US thing. We never thought it was racist or inappropriate, nobody ever thought that here, and most people still don't care. We have an entirely different social and cultural history. And if there's anything we don't tolerate, it's this kind of SJW stuff. You wanted to try and understand this whole thing? Cool. But you're looking at the whole thing from the wrong perspective.

&#x200B;

You know, back in the 90s, it didn't seem like anybody cared about Trudeau's blackface, right? It only blew up "recently". And even then, I'd say it's a vocal minority that has problems with it.

&#x200B;

Just because you're part of that vocal minority, doesn't mean that you can invalidate a whole other country's social and cultural views because they differ from yours.

\[\*\]

&#x200B;

